{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/293642-just-for-fun-goblin-market-and-odd-humans","id":293642,"title":"[Just For Fun] Goblin Market and \"odd humans\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-27T05:38:06-07:00","id":293642,"title":"[Just For Fun] Goblin Market and \"odd humans\"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The requirements one must fulfill to become a Market vendor are strict, but not necessarily in the ways you might expect. First off, the Market doesn\u2019t discriminate based on type. A wide variety of hobgoblins and changelings make up the Market workforce, and, if rumor is to be believed, the stalls include a fallen Gentry or two, a few willworkers, <b>the odd human</b>, and even things further removed from the fae. </div> </div> </div>Literally one thing comes up to my mind. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/D016vx8.jpg?1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Yes, I'm porting Crazy Hassan to my planned Changeling chronicle. And nothing will stop me.<br /> <br /> PS. Share your &quot;atypical&quot; vendors, basically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T00:01:23-07:00","id":294564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/293642-just-for-fun-goblin-market-and-odd-humans#post293642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">few willworkers</div> </div> </div> </div>From when mages knows about Goblin Market and sell stuff there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:00:20-07:00","id":295106,"title":"","content":"Apparently they do, since that's from official book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:40:42-07:00","id":295158,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit shocked, as <b>Mage</b> books only mentioned <b>Changling</b> as &quot;possible myths, sometimes found a beings that could be fae or not&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T14:40:17-07:00","id":295242,"title":"","content":"Some Mages do obsess in Changeling about Arcadia and ask too many questions for the comfort of Changelings. Goddamn stalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T17:37:48-07:00","id":295443,"title":"","content":"In some ways, Crumplethorn is a fairly bog-standard Hob salesman. Physically, he looks as though someone had taken a massive flabby ogre and squashed him down to 3 feet in size, with folds and rolls of loose skin and fat everywhere. When it comes to negotiating a bargain, his acumen is just as sharp as the other vendors, and his wares, a variety of Contracts, are relatively normal, too. <br /> <br /> What's unique about Crumplethorn is the way his customers are given their gifts of dubious provenance. One man is given, in an attempt to learn to channel the Diviner's Madness, a christmas-tree-ornament-sized globe of glass, filled with pulsating light. He is then instructed to insert the globe as a suppository - where it shatters. In the instant where shock turns into pain, the slivers of glass dissolve into icy pinpricks, which flow into the customer's body, filling his mind with power. And later that evening, his toilet glows purple. <br /> <br /> Another is given a pushpin with a smiling face for a head, and instructed to push it squarely into the center of his left eye in order to gain the Sight of Truth and Lies. The pin lodges in the pupil and swiftly turns black, melding so perfectly with his eye that there's no apparent seam - though if you look closely, there's the hint of a smiley face there.<br /> <br /> Is that unusual enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}